                <pb facs="0908" n="1742" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1429W</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-12T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 12, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1418. Instruct consuls in Spain that Department is at present considering plan of
                    bunker control whereby all Spanish line vessels bound for America be required to
                    put in at Porto Rico. This plan proposes bunker arrangement with Spain whereby
                    all passengers on Spanish ships must have passport visés from American consular
                    officers. Present information indicates Mexican consular official, Bilbao, has
                    issued “laisser passer” or permits to enter Mexico, to persons of different
                    nationalities, which documents are in no sense passports, but which have been
                    viséd by Cuban Consul, Bilbao, … and by use of which bearers have obtained
                    passage on Spanish vessels. Person bearing such documents without having
                    passport from government of country of which he is subject should not under any
                    circumstances receive visé if application is made to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
